WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
Morning, John.

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.800
Sometimes I forget that not everyone in America is like me

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.600
and in fact, most people do not live their lives

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.860
on the internet.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.500
Like, there are lots of people in America

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.700
who still have dial-up internet,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.840
who've never streamed a video,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.900
who think that LOL stands for "lots of love",

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.240
which, tangentially, is a very dangerous mistake to make.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.860
It can lead to emails like,

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:21.740
"Dear Lynn,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.640
I was so sorry to hear

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.220
of the passing of your wonderful Golden Retriever.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.980
And it's times like these, that we must take comfort in God's love.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.500
Lol, Margaret."

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.300
So yeah,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.620
Katherine's parents are here visiting

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.629
and they have never had a high-speed internet in their lives.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:41.060
They seem very interested and supportive when I try to explain to them what it is that I do,

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.080
but it's obvious that, more or less,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.760
we're talking different languages.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.500
Honestly, I can't figure out why they're so nice about it.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.240
I mean, if my daughter married a dude who is like,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.020
"Sorry, I can't go out to the lunch

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.260
I have to go talking to a camera

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.980
and flail my arms around."

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.100
I don't think I would be very friendly to that guy

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.440
and I have a 10 megabit per second download.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.129
So they don't get it.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:00.940
But I guess they don't have to

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.480
because they're really nice about it anyway.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.220
So thanks to them for that.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:08.920
Also Katherine's brother and her sister-in-law and their son,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.060
our nephew who's 4 years old,

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.020
are also in town,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.040
which makes for a big group of people.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.020
And John, I have to tell you,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.320
four-year-olds...

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.740
in whatever amount of time between now and when Henry is 4,

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.500
you've got some preparations to do.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.940
Because Bill Cosby was right,

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:28.720
they have

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.660
[Bill Cosby]: Brain damage!

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:30.840
One second, he's like,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:31.949
"Uncle Hank, I love you.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.220
Let's play go fish."

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:33.940
And I'm like,

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.620
"That sounds like a wonderful idea.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.720
Let's play go fish."

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.620
And then five minutes later, I'm like,

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.340
"Do you have any jacks?"

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:41.680
And then he's all,

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.060
[Demon voice]: "I will torture your soul for an eternity of hellfire.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.500
Now sit in awe

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.380
as I make a noise that will kill all the dolphins."

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.780
[Shriek noise]

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.980
But mostly,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.220
you know aside from the dolphin killing,

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.320
he's very fun.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:56.940
Seriously though,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:57.860
we hang out

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:58.360
and we eat

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.320
and he's funny

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.260
and he's cute and

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:04.140
I've been going to sleep way earlier than is natural for my body,

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.440
He wakes up at 6 o'clock in the morning,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.700
every morning.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.720
What kind of demon does that?

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.740
Sleep, friend!

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.140
(sleep!)

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.000
Also, I'm trying to teach him the meaning of words like

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.760
perseverance

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.940
and relaxation.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.800
But ooo...

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.000
he does not get either of those ideas at all.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.520
Trying to get the idea of relaxation across to him

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.300
is very confusing, I think.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.340
It- it's this thing

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.480
that you can do

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.900
that's actually not doing anything.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.540
You just don't do stuff.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.100
You just... chill.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.920
Which does not compute because of the brain damage.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.740
And with perseverance,

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.040
he pretty much would rather not be doing whatever it is he's doing

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.540
and he would like to be doing whatever it is that he

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.520
cannot

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.520
do.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.400
Not allowed!

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.700
Why did this video turn into a video about a four year old?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.300
But I do have to tell you one last thing he is obsessed with:

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.560
his poops.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.560
Particularly with the size of his poops

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.360
and he also assumes that,

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.580
likewise you will be very interested in the size of his poops.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.180
Anyway,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.120
the slow pace of development of human children

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.960
is a side effect of our reliance upon cultural and not genetic evolution

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.000
and that is the very thing that makes people so amazing

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:08.760
and so awesome

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.820
and so unique.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.800
So I guess,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.500
it would be foolish of me to complain about it.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.320
So everybody,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.100
I think that my nephew was curious,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.240
how has your poop been lately?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.160
John,

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.790
I will see you on Monday.

